From: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:09:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Never expose pseudo-elements via Event.target; fix
 ::column disposal

FlyWeb next batch: from branch-heads/8078 f95dd51f6f. Applied after seguridad/portes-159/chromium/0002 (#1159); applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for these files.

Original change's description:
> Never expose pseudo-elements via Event.target; fix ::column disposal
>
> While default event handlers run, an event's target is set back to the
> raw pseudo-element if it has activation behavior (e.g.
> ::scroll-marker), so that its DefaultEventHandler() can recognize
> itself. Script that runs during that time, such as a DOMActivate
> listener, could read the target of a click event it kept and get a live
> PseudoElement. Similarly, coalesced and predicted pointer events have
> their target set to the raw dispatch node. Event::target() only
> DCHECKed against this, so in release builds the pseudo-element was
> handed to script, which could then re-parent it and corrupt the
> pseudo-element tree. Event::target() now returns the ultimate
> originating element when the stored target is a connected
> pseudo-element, and null otherwise.
>
> Disposing a ::column did not dispose its ::scroll-marker, because
> ColumnPseudoElement::DetachLayoutTree() bypasses
> Element::DetachLayoutTree(), which is where other pseudo-elements
> dispose their child pseudo-elements.
> Element::ClearColumnPseudoElements() worked around that by walking the
> live ::column vector first, which is the walk that re-entrancy turned
> into a use-after-free. Other paths, such as
> PseudoElementData::ClearPseudoElements() from
> Element::RecalcOwnStyle(), left the ::scroll-marker connected under a
> disposed ::column (hitting a DCHECK in Element::RemovedFrom()).
> ColumnPseudoElement::Dispose() now disposes its own pseudo-elements,
> Element::ClearColumnPseudoElements() no longer walks the vector, and
> PseudoElementData::ClearColumnPseudoElements() snapshots the elements
> before disposing them, matching
> PseudoElementData::ClearPseudoElements().
>
> column-scroll-marker-reentrant-remove-crash.html covers the
> Event::target() leak (it hit the DCHECK in Event::target() before this
> change). column-scroll-marker-hidden-event-target-crash.html covers the
> ::column disposal (it hit the DCHECK in Element::RemovedFrom() without
> the ColumnPseudoElement::Dispose() change).
>
